# Secrets for the STAGING destination (`kamal deploy -d staging`).
#
# Read alongside .kamal/secrets-common, which holds RAILS_MASTER_KEY,
# RESEND_API_KEY, ADMIN_SEED_PASSWORD and the registry token.
#
# DO NOT ENTER RAW CREDENTIALS HERE. This file is committed. Export
# STAGING_DATABASE_PASSWORD in the deploying shell; nothing is stored here.

# One password, three names, all the same value:
#
#   POSTGRES_PASSWORD
#     read by the postgres image's initdb when the accessory first boots.
#
#   STAGING_DATABASE_PASSWORD
#     read by config/database.yml's staging block on
#     feature/spec-010-email-delivery.
#
#   SYNDICATE_DEVELOPMENT_2026_DATABASE_PASSWORD
#     read by that same block on feature/spec-011-admin-auth, which uses the
#     production variable name instead.
#
# Those two branches disagree and neither is merged. Injecting both app-side
# names means staging authenticates whichever one lands first. Drop the redundant
# one once the branches are reconciled.
STAGING_DATABASE_PASSWORD=$STAGING_DATABASE_PASSWORD
SYNDICATE_DEVELOPMENT_2026_DATABASE_PASSWORD=$STAGING_DATABASE_PASSWORD
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=$STAGING_DATABASE_PASSWORD
